      "body": "At a glance\n\nTransport Fever 3 is Urban Games' newest simulation entry on Steam (AppID 3493540), launching into Early Access on September 29, 2026. This reference hub organizes confirmed launch facts, pre-order and editions information, system requirements, platform support, and the gameplay pages that follow this launch window. Every section links to the source-backed Steam store page so readers can verify changing details as new updates post.\n\nTransport Fever 3 launch status and Early Access window\n\nTransport Fever 3 ships on September 29, 2026 with an Early Access window flag visible on the Steam store page. The launch covers Steam PC at the AppID listed above; console release dates (PlayStation 5, Xbox Series X|S) and Mac release dates are not announced as of 2026-09-28, so this hub records the Steam PC launch and flags the rest as dated uncertainty. The dedicated release date status page tracks any updates that post after launch day.\n\nThe Early Access window flag means players receive the launch build on day one and can expect the development team to publish follow-up updates through the Early Access period. Until then, the Steam store page and Steam Community Hub are the two surfaces where launch-day patch notes will surface first.\n\nPre-order, editions, and Steam store details\n\nThe pre-order guide explains how to reserve a copy on Steam, what ships with the pre-order bonus, and which edition tier matches different player goals. The editions and pricing page breaks down the Standard and Deluxe tiers visible on Steam and records the Collector's, Limited, and Ultimate tiers as not announced as of 2026-09-28. The Steam store reference page records the AppID, developer and publisher fields, supported interface languages, Steam tags, age rating, and community hub link in one place.\n\nFor pricing scope, regional currency and storefront may vary; readers should always reconfirm the price on their local Steam storefront before completing a transaction. This hub intentionally avoids restating the price as a stable global value.\n\nSystem requirements, platform support, and multiplayer\n\nThe system requirements page collects the Steam-listed minimum and recommended PC specs and flags any unannounced figures as dated uncertainty. The platforms page confirms Steam PC as the launch platform and marks console and Mac release status as not announced as of 2026-09-28. The multiplayer page tracks the Online Multiplayer and co-op signals from the Steam listing; matchmaking tier details and party size limits remain unannounced as of the research date.\n\nIf a reader's PC falls between the published tiers, the system requirements page explains which figure is the launch-day reference and which figures will update once the developer publishes the recommended hardware list.\n\nGameplay reference: vehicles, campaign, economy, and wiki\n\nThe vehicle list page organizes the train, tram, bus, truck, plane, and ship categories visible in the launch trailers. The campaign overview explains the Steam-listed campaign mode and flags the specific mission count as not announced as of 2026-09-28. The economy guide covers finances, cargo, passengers, and industries at the surface level without importing economy tables from earlier Transport Fever titles. The wiki and FAQ page links readers back to the Steam store page description and Steam Community Hub for lore and frequently asked questions until a third-party wiki is established.\n\nLegacy Transport Fever titles (Train Fever, Transport Fever, Transport Fever 2) are not current-game sources and appear here only as sibling disambiguation notes, never as fact carriers."
